1
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,480
That is not a CGI.

2
00:00:03,803 --> 00:00:10,183
That's thousands of drones over the river in Chongqing and the whole city came out to watch.

3
00:00:10,574 --> 00:00:13,674
I spent six days here but not as a tourist.

4
00:00:13,925 --> 00:00:16,335
I came on a study mission from Singapore.

5
00:00:16,640 --> 00:00:19,190
government briefings, hospitals,

6
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:20,550
Robot Labs

7
00:00:20,956 --> 00:00:23,886
Doors tourists don't get to walk through.

8
00:00:24,205 --> 00:00:24,725
So

9
00:00:25,115 --> 00:00:26,855
This video does two things.

10
00:00:27,311 --> 00:00:31,411
It answers every question you'll have before you visit Chongqing.

11
00:00:31,794 --> 00:00:34,484
and it shows you what's behind those doors.

12
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:35,750
I'm Shawn

13
00:00:35,879 --> 00:00:38,929
I'm Singaporean and this is Shawn in China.

14
00:00:39,289 --> 00:00:39,879
Let's go.

15
00:00:40,179 --> 00:00:42,419
First question, everyone asked.

16
00:00:42,788 --> 00:00:43,828
Do you need a visa?

17
00:00:44,242 --> 00:00:45,632
If you're Singaporean

18
00:00:46,017 --> 00:00:54,067
Since February 2024, Singapore and China let each other's citizens visit visa-free for up to 30 days.

19
00:00:54,441 --> 00:00:55,501
Not Singaporean.

20
00:00:55,951 --> 00:00:58,971
Check the 240 hour visa free transit

21
00:00:59,443 --> 00:01:02,863
Chongqing's airport is one of the eligible entry points.

22
00:01:03,217 --> 00:01:05,517
As long as you're flying on to a third country.

23
00:01:05,892 --> 00:01:09,372
the rules change. So check the official list before you book.

24
00:01:09,773 --> 00:01:11,003
second question

25
00:01:11,392 --> 00:01:12,192
How do you pay?

26
00:01:12,593 --> 00:01:13,233
Here's the thing.

27
00:01:13,683 --> 00:01:16,573
China barely uses cash or cards in shops.

28
00:01:16,978 --> 00:01:19,198
It runs on Alipay and WeChat Pay.

29
00:01:19,629 --> 00:01:25,309
And both now accept foreign visa and mastercard. Set them up and verify them before you fly.

30
00:01:25,663 --> 00:01:29,533
I used Alipay and WeChat Pay and it worked almost everywhere.

31
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:32,310
Still, carry a bit of cash.

32
00:01:32,656 --> 00:01:33,396
The third

33
00:01:33,800 --> 00:01:38,180
Google, WhatsApp, and Instagram don't work on Chinese networks.

34
00:01:38,622 --> 00:01:40,712
So I recommend downloading Amap

35
00:01:41,019 --> 00:01:43,199
and a translation app before you land.

36
00:01:43,621 --> 00:01:50,671
Then, a welcome dinner. Round table, lazy Susan and a dish every 30 seconds.

37
00:01:51,111 --> 00:01:54,451
I didn't know half of what I was eating. I finished all of it.

38
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:56,110
Quick context.

39
00:01:56,524 --> 00:02:01,244
Because Chongqing confuses everyone, why do people call it the 8D city?

40
00:02:01,583 --> 00:02:04,153
It's built on mountains where two rivers meet.

41
00:02:04,558 --> 00:02:06,078
The Yangtze and Jialing.

42
00:02:06,405 --> 00:02:10,415
There's barely any flat ground. So the city stacks on itself.

43
00:02:10,913 --> 00:02:12,923
roads run over roofs

44
00:02:13,339 --> 00:02:16,909
You walk into a mall on the ground floor and walk out on the eighth.

45
00:02:17,316 --> 00:02:20,406
Your map app has no idea which level you're on.

46
00:02:20,748 --> 00:02:25,938
We started at the planning exhibition gallery, which is basically the city explaining itself.

47
00:02:26,404 --> 00:02:31,934
The whole municipality has around 32 million people and it's about the size of Austria.

48
00:02:32,306 --> 00:02:33,966
Most of that is countryside.

49
00:02:34,308 --> 00:02:36,938
but the core still feels endless.

50
00:02:37,318 --> 00:02:40,198
Then a briefing I didn't expect to find so interesting.

51
00:02:40,559 --> 00:02:44,309
the China Singapore Chongqing Connectivity Initiative.

52
00:02:44,616 --> 00:02:50,106
It's a government to government project, Singapore's third in China after Suzhou and Tianjin.

53
00:02:50,482 --> 00:02:53,642
Finance logistics aviation digital links.

54
00:02:54,067 --> 00:02:57,987
Is why a Singaporean group gets a seat at this tables at all.

55
00:02:58,344 --> 00:03:04,664
Even the hospital we visited that afternoon was Singaporean, Raffles Hospital in the middle of Chongqing.

56
00:03:05,014 --> 00:03:05,564
And at night,

57
00:03:05,936 --> 00:03:06,776
Guanyinqiao

58
00:03:07,126 --> 00:03:11,236
Screens on every building and the whole street out walking.

59
00:03:11,553 --> 00:03:12,243
Day three.

60
00:03:12,603 --> 00:03:14,123
Our group split in two.

61
00:03:14,549 --> 00:03:17,469
Architects went to see urban renewal projects.

62
00:03:17,742 --> 00:03:19,512
I went the healthcare and tech route.

63
00:03:19,955 --> 00:03:22,735
First stop, Liangjiang Life Science City.

64
00:03:23,166 --> 00:03:31,236
picture a whole district planned around medical devices, biotech and digital health. That is what this is.

65
00:03:31,627 --> 00:03:39,527
Then Haifu Medical. They build HIFU machines focused ultrasound that treats tumors without a single cut.

66
00:03:39,976 --> 00:03:41,426
developed here in Chongqing.

67
00:03:41,771 --> 00:03:47,321
And then in the afternoon, everyone back home asked about, are robots really everywhere in China?

68
00:03:53,697 --> 00:03:55,587
The humanoid danced for us.

69
00:03:56,023 --> 00:03:58,393
A robot dog walked around

70
00:03:58,823 --> 00:04:04,263
But what got me wasn't the tricks. It was how normal it was to the people showing us.

71
00:04:04,719 --> 00:04:06,559
To them this is everyday life.

72
00:04:06,977 --> 00:04:07,807
And then dinner.

73
00:04:08,137 --> 00:04:12,687
On the walk there, skewers rolled in spice powder were in Chongqing after all.

74
00:04:13,053 --> 00:04:16,633
And then we ate at a Mongolian style place done up like a yurt.

75
00:04:17,043 --> 00:04:21,353
So there's a big soup of cabbage bubbling away in the middle of the table.

76
00:04:21,707 --> 00:04:26,067
And then the main event, a whole baby lamb roasted in oven.

77
00:04:26,454 --> 00:04:27,574
brought out by the shop.

78
00:04:27,966 --> 00:04:29,936
and you carve it right at the table.

79
00:04:30,312 --> 00:04:33,292
You put your gloves on and pull off the meat with your hands.

80
00:04:33,646 --> 00:04:37,436
No mala this time, just soup, lamb and a lot of toasting.

81
00:04:37,739 --> 00:04:39,789
This might be the best meal we had.

82
00:04:40,122 --> 00:04:43,042
If you think Chongqing is only neon, start here.

83
00:04:43,397 --> 00:04:48,547
Eling number two factory used to print money for China's Central Bank in the 1940s.

84
00:04:48,889 --> 00:04:54,889
Now it's murals, cafes and studios. And yes, that's a PlayStation controller on a wall.

85
00:04:55,223 --> 00:04:58,593
In the afternoon, the connectivity initiative exhibition hall.

86
00:04:58,948 --> 00:05:02,988
Seeing Singapore's leaders on the wall in Chongqing hit differently.

87
00:05:03,286 --> 00:05:08,206
Then a trade conference. Singapore and Chongqing businesses trying to find each other.

88
00:05:08,508 --> 00:05:11,888
And then the night everyone comes for. Hongyadong.

89
00:05:16,183 --> 00:05:22,623
It's a cliffside complex of stilt houses lit gold and people say it looks like spirited away.

90
00:05:22,933 --> 00:05:23,873
But when should you go?

91
00:05:24,207 --> 00:05:25,017
After dark

92
00:05:25,364 --> 00:05:31,264
The usual advice is to skip the 7:30 p.m. crush and aim for after 8.

93
00:05:31,673 --> 00:05:34,393
Honestly, it's still just as crowded, but

94
00:05:34,768 --> 00:05:36,808
It's a once in a lifetime opportunity.

95
00:05:37,095 --> 00:05:38,275
Is it safe at night?

96
00:05:38,721 --> 00:05:40,681
From everything I saw, yes.

97
00:05:41,110 --> 00:05:45,470
Families out late, people everywhere, just mind your phone in the crowds.

98
00:05:45,885 --> 00:05:47,995
and stand on the riverside and look back

99
00:05:48,411 --> 00:05:51,441
That's the 8D city in one view.

100
00:05:51,746 --> 00:05:54,466
Day five was the nerdy day.

101
00:05:54,835 --> 00:05:57,355
Ever heard of East Data West Computing?

102
00:05:57,737 --> 00:06:00,387
China's richest cities are on the east coast.

103
00:06:00,820 --> 00:06:03,180
And so it's most of the demand for computing

104
00:06:03,559 --> 00:06:06,009
But land and power are cheaper out west.

105
00:06:06,420 --> 00:06:11,810
So the country is building huge data centers like Chongqing to do the computing for the east.

106
00:06:12,117 --> 00:06:13,457
We visited one

107
00:06:13,622 --> 00:06:17,162
No filming was allowed. So here's a group photo.

108
00:06:17,451 --> 00:06:24,301
The other theme that week was aging. China has more than 300 million people over 60.

109
00:06:24,557 --> 00:06:25,637
Across the trip

110
00:06:25,821 --> 00:06:30,951
We saw how companies here use AI and digital tools for elder care and health.

111
00:06:31,348 --> 00:06:34,378
Singapore is aging too, so I took a lot of notes.

112
00:06:34,796 --> 00:06:38,856
That evening, finally, proper Chongqing hotpot.

113
00:06:39,268 --> 00:06:44,368
So the honest answer to how spicy is Chongqing hotpot? Very spicy.

114
00:06:44,722 --> 00:06:49,672
It's mala. So the chili burns and the Sichuan pepper numbs your mouth at the same time.

115
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:55,350
My tip is to order a yuanyang pot, split down the middle with a mild broth on one side.

116
00:06:55,793 --> 00:06:57,253
No one judges you.

117
00:06:57,602 --> 00:06:58,732
Maybe just a little

118
00:06:59,102 --> 00:07:00,062
Then, food street.

119
00:07:00,517 --> 00:07:02,307
What should I eat besides hotpot?

120
00:07:02,771 --> 00:07:04,111
Jiefangbei Food Street

121
00:07:04,578 --> 00:07:08,168
Skewers, Chongqing noodles, snacks I couldn't name.

122
00:07:08,597 --> 00:07:09,587
If there's a queue

123
00:07:09,819 --> 00:07:10,339
join it.

124
00:07:15,753 --> 00:07:18,453
Is it expensive? Not compared with Singapore.

125
00:07:18,803 --> 00:07:23,743
Last morning, a reflection session where we shared what we'd take back to Singapore.

126
00:07:24,088 --> 00:07:27,918
Then I had one afternoon for myself and I did all the tourist things.

127
00:07:28,341 --> 00:07:36,811
Getting around is easier than it looks. The metro and monorail are cheap and yes, at Liziba the train does really does go through a residential building.

128
00:07:37,215 --> 00:07:39,695
Wear good shoes because there are stairs everywhere.

129
00:07:40,059 --> 00:07:42,739
A few friends took the cableway over the Yangtze

130
00:07:43,181 --> 00:07:46,511
An uncle was writing characters on the pavement with water

131
00:07:46,869 --> 00:07:51,909
Of course there's folding phones too, and there's a hot pot inside an old air raid shelter.

132
00:07:52,267 --> 00:07:53,937
Because of course there is.

133
00:07:56,819 --> 00:08:00,139
So is a study trip worth it compared with traveling on your own?

134
00:08:00,522 --> 00:08:01,242
definitely.

135
00:08:01,592 --> 00:08:02,862
You get rooms you can't book.

136
00:08:03,350 --> 00:08:06,660
And you come home with a group chat full of people who were in the room with you.

137
00:08:07,021 --> 00:08:10,861
The program I went on is Ngee Ann Polytechnic's Travel and Learn to Chongqing.

138
00:08:11,252 --> 00:08:15,662
If you're a Singaporean, it's SkillsFuture supported and accommodations included.

139
00:08:16,080 --> 00:08:18,090
Check the next intake through the link below.

140
00:08:18,505 --> 00:08:19,275
When should you go?

141
00:08:19,678 --> 00:08:21,098
Spring or autumn

142
00:08:21,476 --> 00:08:24,526
Summer is very hot. I went in mid October.

143
00:08:24,830 --> 00:08:27,050
Got a question about Chongqing I didn't answer?

144
00:08:27,479 --> 00:08:28,829
Leave it in the comments.

145
00:08:28,932 --> 00:08:30,272
I'll answer the best ones.

146
00:08:30,682 --> 00:08:34,912
I'm Shawn, this is Shawn in China, and I'll see you in the next city.

